From 895eb6d805e531d44a0a0acc1e3847b2d4fc898b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:09:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0091 -- skip Present() entirely when the
 frame is unchanged

Operator-directed investigation of present_update_window's own
~22-25ms/call real-hardware cost. Read the actual mechanism first:
SDL_UpdateWindowSurface() (SDL_video.c) always wraps
SDL_UpdateWindowSurfaceRects() with a single full-window rect, and the
DOS backend's LFB path (SDL_dosframebuffer.c's
DOSVESA_UpdateWindowFramebuffer) already has dirty-rect dispatch logic
from an earlier DOSKUTSU wave (patch 0033) but always takes the full
SDL_memcpy(fb_state.vram_ptr, fb_state.pixels, fb_state.fb_size)
branch because it never receives a real partial rect list -- AGS's own
Present() never provides one. 307200 bytes get copied every single
call regardless of whether anything actually changed.

Rather than build full sub-window dirty-rect tracking (a much larger
change to RenderToBackBuffer(), flagged as a gap all the way back in
the first round of this whole investigation but never revisited),
this takes the simpler, still-real win: cache the last-presented
frame's raw pixel content and skip BOTH the blit and
SDL_UpdateWindowSurface() entirely when the new frame is byte-
identical to it, the palette did not change (SyncPaletteIfNeeded() now
returns whether it actually changed anything), and xoff/yoff/flip
match the cached call's own. Restricted to the case with no flip and
no border/offset (dst fills the whole window) -- anything else always
falls through to the normal path and invalidates the cache, so
arbitrary window configurations remain correct, just without this
specific skip.

present_dirty_check brackets the comparison's own cost (paid every
"clean case" present); present_skip_unchanged's own calls= count is
how many times the skip actually fired.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014hnodGZ6cg8CWuFXEDTsUq
